title: bin/ scripts stale at $VERSION 1.107 vs lib/ at 1.108
updated: 2026-09-01T04:03:48Z
---

grep -rh "our \$VERSION" lib bin | sort -u yields TWO lines instead of one:

  bin/kube_client:10  our $VERSION = '1.107';
  bin/kube_watch:10   our $VERSION = '1.107';
  (all 40 lib/*.pm files correctly at 1.108)

Root cause (found via git log): commit baf2fbe "increment $VERSION after 1.107 release" (the BumpVersionAfterRelease auto-commit) bumped all 41 lib/ files 1.107 -> 1.108 but did not touch bin/kube_client / bin/kube_watch. This happened before too - an earlier commit message explicitly notes "Also carries the $VERSION bump to 1.107 in bin/kube_client and bin/kube_watch" as a manual follow-up, implying the automated bump does not cover bin/ and someone has to remember to do it by hand every release.

Mitigating: verified `dzil build` DOES correctly rewrite bin/'s $VERSION to 1.108 in the build output (RewriteVersion::Transitional overwrites at build time regardless of the committed source value) - the shipped tarball would NOT actually be broken this time. But the committed source is inconsistent, fails the release-checker's consistency check verbatim, and will drift again next release unless bin/ is bumped by hand or the [@Author::GETTY] BumpVersionAfterRelease file-finder is fixed to include bin/.

Fix: bump bin/kube_client and bin/kube_watch $VERSION to 1.108 before release; consider whether BumpVersionAfterRelease config should cover bin/ automatically going forward.

No fix applied - audit only.
